From: sostk
Subject: [PATCH] GStreamer: pass ring-buffer-max-size as guint64

urisourcebin's "ring-buffer-max-size" is a guint64 property, but WebKit passed
2 * MB, an int, through g_object_set()'s varargs. On 32-bit ARM (EABI) the
64-bit value is read from an aligned register pair and the next property name
from whatever follows on the stack: g_object_set_valist() then looks up a
garbage pointer and the web process crashes (SIGSEGV, fault address 0x1, in
param_spec_pool_hash) when an MSE/blob: video is set up with playbin3.

---
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
@@ -2739,7 +2739,7 @@ void MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer::configureElement(GstElement* element)
     // mode. Some demuxers (matroskademux) don't work as well in push mode.
     if (startsWith(name.span(), "urisourcebin"_s) && !m_isLegacyPlaybin && m_preload == MediaPlayer::Preload::Auto) {
         if (isBlob)
-            g_object_set(element, "ring-buffer-max-size", 2 * MB, nullptr);
+            g_object_set(element, "ring-buffer-max-size", static_cast<guint64>(2 * MB), nullptr);
         else if (!isMediaSource() && !isMediaStreamPlayer())
             g_object_set(element, "download", TRUE, nullptr);
     }
